message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Bounded Adaptive Coherence: a coupling-tensor λ_min criterion as a computational object for aging-versus-cancer failure modes"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Can the Principle of Bounded Adaptive Coherence — λ_min(C(t)) against
  scale-wise entropy production — be stated as a falsifiable computational
  object such that aging-like global coupling decay and cancer-like selective
  organism-scale decoupling appear as distinct sectors of the same tensor,
  without claiming clinical rejuvenation or cure? On a five-index toy, the
  literal minimum eigenvalue of the raw coupling matrix moves the wrong way
  as coupling strengthens. The object used instead is the minimum eigenvalue
  of a grounded Laplacian of the symmetric weights, minus a declared proxy.
  Global decay and an organism-index cut fall in different predeclared
  classes. Uneven decay, diagonal-only decay, and a held matrix do not.
  Not a medical device. No rejuvenation claim. No cure.
keywords:
